    <statement><p>Find:</p>
<p>(a)
<m>\lim\limits_{t\to-\infty}\, (\frac{1}{t^{2}}+3) =</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><em>(Enter the word <alert>infinity</alert> or <alert>-infinity</alert>
if the limit goes to <m>\infty</m> or <m>-\infty</m>.)</em></p>
<p>(b)
<m>\lim\limits_{t\to\infty}\, 3\frac{1}{y} =</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><em>(Enter the word <alert>infinity</alert> or <alert>-infinity</alert>
if the limit goes to <m>\infty</m> or <m>-\infty</m>.)</em></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\lim\limits_{t\to-\infty}\, \frac{1}{t^{2}}+3 = \lim\limits_{t\to-\infty}\frac{1}{t^2} + 3 = 0 + 3 = 3</m>.




(b)
<m>\lim\limits_{y\to\infty}\, 3\frac{1}{y} = \lim\limits_{y\to\infty}\,\frac{3}{y^1} = 0</m>.



</solution>
